comments.body:
Another alternative is a helper that appends an output and returns its index:

```cpp
std::vector<CTxOut> outputs;
const auto add_output{[&](CTxOut out) {
    outputs.push_back(std::move(out));
    return uint32_t(outputs.size() - 1);
}};

const uint32_t sixteen_sigops_idx{add_output(CTxOut{5000, GetScriptForDestination(ScriptHash(sixteenSigops))})};

CMutableTransaction txFrom;
txFrom.vout = std::move(outputs);
AddCoins(coins, CTransaction(txFrom), 0);
```

Then the spending transactions can use `sixteen_sigops_idx` instead of `5`.

